  "label": "Irony and Absurdity as Comedic Device",
  "description": "The humor of the meme stems from the absurdity of a child asking a profound spiritual question in a context that is physically messy and childish. This relies on the understanding of irony — saying something that is the opposite of what is intended — and the comedic effect of absurdity, which is a recognized technique in humor and satire.",
